## Why This Is Asked

Introduces bias and fairness in a practical recommender task with limited labels and a new user base.

## Key Concepts

- Fairness metrics: demographic parity, equalized odds
- Calibration under limited labels
- Simple baselines: logistic regression, small decision trees
- Data splits and leakage avoidance
- Lightweight retraining and drift monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple group CTR calculator
function groupCTR(data, group) {
  const g = data.filter(d => d.group === group);
  const clicks = g.filter(d => d.clicked).length;
  return g.length ? clicks / g.length : 0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend with per-group debiasing?
- How would you validate fairness on unseen regions?

