Why This Is Asked
- Tests ability to design robust, low-latency hybrid ML systems under distribution shift.
- Probes gating, calibration, drift handling, and online experimentation.

Key Concepts
- Hybrid models, gating mechanisms, calibration, drift detection, online A/B testing, latency budgets.

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for gating logic
function route(transaction, gateModel, fastDetector, autoencoder) {
  const uncertainty = gateModel.predict(transaction);
  if (uncertainty > THRESHOLD) return autoencoder.detect(transaction);
  return fastDetector.detect(transaction);
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift windows and decide retraining cadence?
- How would you securely log data for online experimentation and ensure latency budgets are met?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design for real-time fraud scoring at scale with privacy constraints, multi-tenant data sharing, and safe rollbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming feature store and time-window features
- Hybrid inference paths: server-side and on-device
- Federated learning with differential privacy
- Drift detection and canary-based rollout strategies
- Model calibration and per-transaction explainability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo scoring sketch
function score(tx, globalModel, localModel){
  const feats = extract(tx)
  const s1 = globalModel.predict(feats)
  const s2 = localModel.predict(feats)
  return calibrate((0.6*s1 + 0.4*s2));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle label latency for online updates?
- What metrics trigger rollback and how would you test rollbacks?
